# PoC run 2 (-memory old), STRONGER variant: recover y outright.
# Same program as ../scale-mamba/Programs/attack_recover (FANNG is a fork).
#
# The analysis is "checking d = y - b on its own": with an off-key mask b
# (fresh, authenticated under alpha+1) and the carried secret y (authenticated
# under alpha), the unmasked MAC check opens the value d*(alpha+1) - m_d = g - y.
# FANNG-MPC inherits SCALE-MAMBA's unmasked check, so the attacker reads y directly.
#
# We open that d = y - b on its own -- a single opening -- so the batched check
# value is exactly r*(g - y) with a single, attacker-known coefficient r, and the
# instrumented check inverts it to y = g - t/r (see patches/offkey_recover.py).
# b comes from a fresh preprocessed square tuple, so it is authenticated under
# the current run's key; between runs the attacker set that key to alpha+1.
#
# Nothing about y is revealed by the opened value d itself: b is uniform and
# independent, so d = y - b is uniform. The leak is purely through the unmasked
# check value, which the attacker recovers before the run aborts.
y = sint.load_mem(100)
b, _ = sint.get_random_square()   # b: fresh mask, authenticated under alpha+1
d = (y - b).reveal()              # single off-key opening d = y - b
print_ln("d = %s (uniform; reveals nothing about y on its own)", d)
